  "body": [
    "Four families of machine, each tuned by hand for a different kind of morning. Start with how you like to make it — we'll help you find the rest.",
    "Bean-to-cup · Premium",
    "Whole beans in, a finished cup out — milk, timing and all. The most hands-off way to drink well, and the only machines that actually learn your taste.",
    "The Atelier learns and adapts on its own; the Mini carries the same brain to a smaller counter.",
    "It senses what you like, builds a taste profile, reads the day ahead and pours accordingly — quietly taking care of the rest.",
    "Learns your taste cup by cup, no dialing-in",
    "Reads your calendar and mood to pace the morning",
    "Reorders beans before you run out",
    "The same clever heart, sized for smaller kitchens.",
    "Espresso",
    "Grind, tamp, pull. Machines for people who want to be the barista — precise, tactile, and built to reward practice.",
    "The Barista gives you full manual control; the Everyday keeps it simple for a reliable shot each morning.",
    "A hands-on machine for the morning ritualist.",
    "Honest espresso, every single morning.",
    "Filter",
    "Clean, balanced filter coffee for the unhurried cup — the kind you sip through a quiet morning.",
    "One machine, perfected: even saturation and gentle timing, so every batch tastes the same.",
    "Filter coffee, unhurried and beautifully even.",
    "Cold brew",
    "Smooth, low-acid cold brew steeped overnight — poured cold straight from the fridge.",
    "Set it before bed; the Carafe does the steeping while you sleep.",
    "Smooth cold brew, ready and waiting by morning."
  ],
